  "id": "COMPOUND:30135 - PROTEIN:6150",
  "verbalization": "Tenacissoside B appears to be a potential modulator of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 through a series of target relationships. The evidence suggests that Tenacissoside B acts as a target for Prelamin-A/C, which in turn is targeted by Oleamide and Diplotrin A. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, indicating a possible pathway where Tenacissoside B may influence this transporter via the intermediaries of Prelamin-A/C, Oleamide, and Diplotrin A. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a plausible mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains to be elucidated. The integration of these targets implies that Tenacissoside B may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the regulation of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, possibly by modulating the expression or activity of the intermediaries. This relationship is supported by the presence of a well-defined target hierarchy, which aligns with the persona's expectation of a clinically proven drug–disease link or a well-documented mode of action.",
